From 313568f3373dd4dfaac094cead6de5ef2cc3d12e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The browser Authors <noreply@browser.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:40:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 34/61] ai-parity

The built-in AI APIs answer as Chrome does, though this build ships no
on-device model service: LanguageModel and Summarizer are downloadable
where Chrome's own CPU rule admits the machine (15000 MB as
navigator.deviceMemory reports it, 4 processors), and downloading once a
page has started the download. create() without a user gesture fails as
in Chrome; with one it waits on a download that never finishes, its
monitor told the first progress (0). LanguageDetector uses Chrome's
language detection model, which the build copies from the Chromium source
(components/test/data/translate/valid_model.tflite) to LanguageDetection/
beside the browser and packaging ships: downloadable until startup is
complete, then available, as on a Chrome profile that has the model.
